+# DRAFT H — integration service scope; NOT APPROVED
+
+Bind each key credential_id to an immutable registered service principal, then
+explicit allowed operations, client IDs, products and canonical tenant UUIDs.
+Reject missing registrations, unknown scopes and tenant/product mismatches.
+A mutable IntegrationAPIKey.name or a caller supplied client_id cannot establish
+that authority. Configured fallback credentials need the same principal binding.
+
+Introspection must intersect the authenticated service registration with the
+verified token context; product validation and legacy identity endpoints must
+apply their own operation/tenant/product permission. No wildcard is implicit.
+
+Approve central-service cross-tenant exceptions individually with audit and
+expiry. Inventory ISO Smart and MedSupplier keys first; plan compatibility,
+rotation, revocation, audit failure behavior and migration from global keys.
+Acceptance includes same-key cross-product and cross-tenant denial, revoked or
+rotated keys, DatabaseError at authentication/audit, and no permissive fallback.
+No grants, key rotations, schema or deployment are authorized by this draft.
